    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field on the owner response, derived from the owner's locality/region via a fixed region-to-timezone table (IANA names):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` string property (readOnly) to the Owner schema, right after `locality`, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/Regions.java`** \u2014 Added a fixed `REGION_TIMEZONES` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneForRegion(String)` method that returns the IANA name, or `null` for a null/unknown region.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` mapping backed by a new `formatTimezone(owner)` method that maps the owner's locality (via `formatLocality`) through `Regions.timezoneForRegion`.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` \u2014 Sydney/postcode 2000 \u2192 locality `NSW`, timezone `Australia/Sydney`) and the full test suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
