    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is placed exactly where the existing conventions dictate and reuses them cleanly:\n\n- The region\u2192timezone table (`REGION_TIMEZONES`) lives in `Regions` right beside the analogous `REGION_RANGES` table, and the lookup (`timezoneForRegion`) mirrors the existing `forPostcode` static accessor \u2014 same style, same null handling, same Javadoc shape.\n- `formatTimezone` in `OwnerMapper` mirrors the sibling `format*` default methods exactly: null-owner guard, one-line delegation, consistent Javadoc. It correctly derives the region by reusing `formatLocality(owner)` rather than re-deriving it, so there's no duplicated region logic.\n- The `@Mapping` entry is slotted next to the related `locality` mapping, and the OpenAPI `timezone` field is added alongside the region field with a matching description/example.\n\nNo logic is misplaced, nothing is duplicated, and neither `Regions` nor `OwnerMapper` is becoming a catch-all \u2014 the mapper is already the established home for these derived DTO fields. A maintainer would find this natural.",
